DESCRIPTION:Grow the Grasslands in Toronto's High Park				\n				\n				\n				\n									Wednesday\, June 3\, 2026\, 6:30-8:30PM Ages: 16+ years 								\n				\n					\n		\n				\n			\n							\n		\n					\n		\n				\n						\n					\n			\n						\n				\n									NOTE: Pre-registration is required for all our events\, hikes and workshops. We do this to ensure we don’t exceed our capacity for indoor events or the maximum limits for group sizes on High Park’s ecologically sensitive trails. Please register on our website before coming to High Park. We cannot guarantee availability of walk-in spots. If an event is at capacity\, please put yourself on our waitlist. We will notify waitlisted participants if we open up new spots or sessions for our events. Please contact us if you have any questions. 								\n				\n				\n				\n					Grow the Grasslands in Toronto's High Park				\n				\n				\n				\n									Get your hands in the soil and be part of something taking root across the country. Join us for a community planting event to grow the Black Oak Savannah in High Park: one of Toronto’s most endangered ecosystems and part of a much larger grassland story stretching across Canada. As we plant native species together\, you’ll learn how these landscapes support biodiversity\, store carbon\, and connect to conservation efforts nationwide through the Canadian Grasslands Coalition. Whether you’re a seasoned gardener or just sprouting\, this is your chance to take meaningful action\, meet your community\, and leave a lasting impact. Spots are limited and the grasslands are waiting for you. Price: FREEAges: 16+ yearsMeeting Location: High Park Forest School\, 375 Colborne Lodge Drive 								\n				\n				\n				\n									\n					\n						\n									Register Now\n					\n					\n				\n								\n				\n					\n		\n					\n		\n				\n						\n					\n			\n						\n				\n					About the Canadian Grassland CoalitionThe Canadian Grassland Coalition is a collaborative network of individuals and organizations — not-for-profits\, educators\, scientists\, Indigenous voices\, producers\, governments — across Canada that are passionate about grasslands. We all work in our own region(s)\, with stakeholders\, towards the conservation of natural grasslands. Together we are a collective force advocating for the magnificence of grasslands\, their value to Canadians\, the threats they face\, and the solutions to ensure that these precious landscapes remain vibrant\, resilient\, and full of life for generations to come. 				\n				\n				\n				\n									\n					\n						\n									Learn more\n					\n					\n				\n								\n				\n					\n		\n					\n		\n				\n						\n					\n			\n						\n				\n																														\n				\n				\n				\n																														\n				\n				\n						\n					\n			\n							\n		\n				\n			\n						\n				\n							\n							\n					\n												\n															\n								\n													\n												Date & Time\n					\n\n					Day: Wednesday\, June 3Time: 6:30-8:30PM\n				\n							\n					\n												\n															\n								\n													\n												Location\n					\n\n					This event will start at the High Park Forest School building located at 375 Colborne Lodge Drive. A number of changes were made to the travel network within High Park as part of the High Park Movement Strategy that might influence your decision to drive to High Park. In case you’re driving we strongly recommend you to park your car at the public parking lot near Grenadier Cafe. We continue to recommend using the TTC or biking as the best way to get to High Park and the Nature Centre. The Nature Centre is situated just a 5-minute walk from the High Park Subway Station. Please note\, High Park is closed to cars on the weekends. If your event is on a weekend\, you will need to park outside the park and walk in\, or take transit. Visit our How To Get Here page to learn more about planning your trips to High Park. \n				\n							\n					\n												\n															\n								\n													\n												Price\n					\n\n					General Admission (Seniors\,  Adults and Youth): FREE\n				\n							\n					\n												\n															\n								\n													\n												Ages\n					\n\n					This event is for youth and adults ages 16 years and above. \n				\n							\n					\n												\n															\n								\n													\n												Accessibility\n					\n\n					Hike routes through High Park might include some uneven terrain and mild slopes. The High Park Forest School building is not yet an AODA-compliant facility. We try our best to accommodate accessibility needs on a case-by-case basis. Please reach out to us about any accessibility-related questions you might have. \n				\n							\n					\n												\n															\n								\n													\n												Dogs\, Pets and Service Animals\n					\n\n					Dogs and other pets are not permitted in our programs. However\, certified service animals\, such as registered therapy or guide dogs\, are welcome. \n				\n								\n						\n				\n				\n				\n									\n					\n						\n									Register Now\n					\n					\n				\n								\n				\n					\n		\n				\n			\n							\n		\n					\n		\n					\n		\n					\n		\n				\n					\n			\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n		\n				\n			\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n		\n					\n					\n			\n						\n				\n					Registration Policies 				\n				\n				\n				\n									Please ensure you’ve read and understood our registration policies:								\n				\n				\n				\n							\n							\n											\n													\n										General Cancellation Policy\n									\n								\n											\n													\n										Extreme Weather-Related Cancellation Policy\n									\n								\n											\n													\n										Behaviour Policy\n									\n						\n						\n				\n				\n				\n									\n					\n						\n									Read Our Registration Policies
URL:https://highparknaturecentre.com/event/sp26-may-birding-walk-01/
LOCATION:High Park Forest School\, 375 Colborne Lodge Drive\, Toronto\, ON\, M6P 3K8\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Nature Hike,Special Events,Stewardship
